internal-vocab bin/pi_taxonomy.py KNOWN_DOMAINS is the seam's documented default example set (five domain names from the box this grew up on). It is a DEFAULT, read at call time and overridable via FLEET_DOMAINS; deleting the names would delete the evidence the override test is built on, which is why the change here was a seam rather than a deletion.

internal-vocab bin/fleet_pid_assert.py NAME_STRIP_PREFIXES is box-local name-repair data: a worktree directory is `<repo>-<session name>`, and these are this box's repo names. It is a named constant and not a "strip the first path segment" rule on purpose — a blanket strip over-matches and can witness the wrong live session. Widening it to a generic default is a behaviour change U8 is not authorised to make silently, so it is reported upward instead of guessed at.

internal-vocab bin/test_*.py 24 test modules use this box's real session names as fixture data for the lineage, door, domain-cap, index and identity tests. The assertions are ABOUT those names (legacy `domain-` prefixes resolving to a domain, drift between a tmux name and a pi name, a pinned baseline of 7 rows); renaming them would delete the evidence the tests are built on rather than sanitise it. Covers: test_fleet_ack, audit, bundle, children, dismiss_semantics, domain_cap, door, entries, gate, identity, integrity, lineage, p0, policy, reconcile, restore, resume_dark, scrub, sweep_lineage, test_name_contract, test_pi_identity, test_pi_index, test_pi_taxonomy, test_pi_view.

internal-vocab docs/SCAFFOLD-NOTES.md This file IS the measurement report of what was copied out of this box: its whole content is tables of per-file counts of this box's own private vocabulary. Sanitising it would destroy the record the U2 unit was asked to produce. It is deliberately excluded from the published tarball (`package.json` files: `!docs/SCAFFOLD-NOTES.md`), so it never reaches an npm consumer.

